WEBVTT

00:00.422 --> 00:03.635
- [Voiceover] Bob is riding his
bicycle along the same path.

00:03.635 --> 00:05.348
For zero is less than or equal to t

00:05.348 --> 00:06.658
is less than or equal to 10.

00:06.658 --> 00:10.176
Bob's velocity is modeled
by B of t is equal to

00:10.176 --> 00:12.834
t to the third minus
six t squared plus 300,

00:12.834 --> 00:16.143
where t is measured in minutes
and B of t is measured in

00:16.143 --> 00:17.733
meters per minute.

00:17.733 --> 00:22.191
Find Bob's acceleration
at time t equals five.

00:22.191 --> 00:23.515
Well acceleration,

00:23.515 --> 00:25.724
this is a velocity
function right over here,

00:25.724 --> 00:27.407
so the acceleration is
going to be derivative

00:27.407 --> 00:29.781
of the velocity function
with respect to time.

00:29.781 --> 00:32.199
What is the rate of change of
velocity with respect to time?

00:32.199 --> 00:33.465
That's acceleration.

00:33.465 --> 00:38.465
So we really just want to evaluate this,

00:38.516 --> 00:41.594
Bob's acceleration at t equals five,

00:41.594 --> 00:45.112
that's going to be B prime of five.

00:45.112 --> 00:47.685
So let's first figure
out what B prime of t is.

00:47.685 --> 00:50.239
B prime of t is equal to,

00:50.239 --> 00:51.203
we'll take the derivative here.

00:51.203 --> 00:52.201
It's pretty straightforward.

00:52.201 --> 00:53.559
Just use the Power Rule.

00:53.559 --> 00:58.559
So it's going to be three
t squared minus 12t,

00:58.850 --> 01:02.507
two times negative six
is 12 or negative 12,

01:02.507 --> 01:05.444
and then the derivative
of 300 doesn't change

01:05.444 --> 01:06.182
with respect to time,

01:06.182 --> 01:07.634
so it's just a zero.

01:07.634 --> 01:12.124
And so B prime of five is
going to be equal to three

01:12.124 --> 01:17.124
times five squared minus 12 times five

01:17.258 --> 01:21.319
which is equal to 75 minus 60

01:21.319 --> 01:23.340
which is equal to 15,

01:23.340 --> 01:25.371
and the units here, this is acceleration.

01:25.371 --> 01:26.370
So this is going to be,

01:26.370 --> 01:28.750
his velocity was in meters per minute,

01:28.750 --> 01:30.358
and so this is going meters per minute,

01:30.358 --> 01:31.503
per minute because remember,

01:31.503 --> 01:33.058
time is in terms of minutes.

01:33.058 --> 01:35.845
So we could write as meters,

01:35.845 --> 01:38.632
and we write it out meters per minute,

01:38.632 --> 01:43.053
per minute which is the same
thing as meters per minute,

01:43.053 --> 01:45.897
meters per minute squared.

01:45.897 --> 01:48.518
All right. Let's do the next part.

01:48.518 --> 01:50.603
Based on the model B from part c,

01:50.603 --> 01:54.260
find Bob's average velocity
during the interval

01:54.260 --> 01:56.184
from zero is less than or equal to t

01:56.184 --> 01:57.669
is less than or equal to 10.

01:57.669 --> 01:59.981
And if the notion of average velocity

01:59.981 --> 02:03.149
or average value of a function
is completely foreign to you,

02:03.149 --> 02:04.533
I encourage you to watch the videos

02:04.533 --> 02:08.191
on Khan Academy on find
the average of a function.

02:08.191 --> 02:12.114
But just to kind of cut to the chase,

02:12.114 --> 02:14.368
the average velocity,

02:14.368 --> 02:15.955
the average velocity,

02:15.955 --> 02:19.217
is going to be the area
under the velocity curve

02:19.217 --> 02:22.433
divided by our change in time.

02:22.433 --> 02:26.474
So the area under the velocity
curve from t equals zero

02:26.474 --> 02:30.351
to t equals 10 of B of t

02:30.351 --> 02:33.579
of B of t, dt,

02:33.579 --> 02:36.714
divided by our change in time.

02:36.714 --> 02:38.216
So it's going to be divided by,

02:38.216 --> 02:39.946
well you're going from zero to 10.

02:39.946 --> 02:43.800
So 10 minus zero is
going to be equal to 10.

02:43.800 --> 02:46.362
And if you wanted the
intuition here it's like well,

02:46.362 --> 02:48.589
if you know the area of
something and if you wanted

02:48.589 --> 02:50.524
to find its average height,

02:50.524 --> 02:52.917
you could just divide by its width.

02:52.917 --> 02:54.195
And that's what we're doing here.

02:54.195 --> 02:56.203
If we know the area of something,

02:56.203 --> 02:58.450
we want to figure out its average height,

02:58.450 --> 03:00.354
and so you divide by its width.

03:00.354 --> 03:03.071
That's I guess a very
high-level intuition for

03:03.071 --> 03:05.637
where this expression came from.

03:05.637 --> 03:08.795
And so this is going to be
equal to one tenth times

03:08.795 --> 03:11.314
the integral from zero to 10,

03:11.314 --> 03:16.314
and B of t is t to the
third power minus 6t squared

03:18.710 --> 03:22.390
plus 300 dt,

03:22.390 --> 03:25.792
and so this is going to
be equal to one over 10.

03:25.792 --> 03:27.208
Take the anti-derivative here,

03:27.208 --> 03:29.832
so this is going to be t
to the fourth over four,

03:29.832 --> 03:32.618
t to the fourth over four,

03:32.618 --> 03:34.453
and then this is going to be,

03:34.453 --> 03:36.295
if we increase the exponent here by

03:36.295 --> 03:37.503
what is t to the third,

03:37.503 --> 03:39.140
and then you divide by three.

03:39.140 --> 03:41.420
So it's negative six divided by three is

03:41.420 --> 03:44.578
negative two, t to the third,

03:44.578 --> 03:47.886
and then plus 300t,

03:47.886 --> 03:49.581
300t,

03:49.581 --> 03:51.938
And I'm going to evaluate it.

03:51.938 --> 03:56.938
I am going to evaluate it
at 10 and subtract from that

03:57.186 --> 03:58.927
and evaluate it at zero.

03:58.927 --> 04:01.482
And so this is going to be equal to,

04:01.482 --> 04:03.950
this is going to be equal to one tenth,

04:03.950 --> 04:05.552
that same one tenth there,

04:05.552 --> 04:07.828
and when you evaluate all this at 10

04:07.828 --> 04:08.971
what'd everybody get?

04:08.971 --> 04:12.708
Let's see 10 to the fourth power is,

04:12.708 --> 04:17.708
10 to the fourth power is
10,000 divided by four is 2,500,

04:18.491 --> 04:20.388
2,500,

04:20.388 --> 04:23.209
and then minus two times 10 to the third.

04:23.209 --> 04:25.420
So it's two times a thousand.

04:25.420 --> 04:28.206
So minus 2,000.

04:28.206 --> 04:30.308
And then 300 times 10,

04:30.308 --> 04:33.059
well that's plus 3,000,

04:33.059 --> 04:35.764
and then you subtract all
of this evaluated at zero

04:35.764 --> 04:37.877
which is just going to be zero.

04:37.877 --> 04:39.898
So this going to be equal to,

04:39.898 --> 04:43.741
2,500 minus 2,000 is 500 plus 3,000.

04:43.741 --> 04:44.786
This is all,

04:44.786 --> 04:47.398
simplifies to 3,500,

04:47.398 --> 04:49.220
or 3,500,

04:49.220 --> 04:50.846
and then you divide it by 10.

04:50.846 --> 04:54.590
This is going to be 350,

04:54.590 --> 04:55.771
350,

04:55.771 --> 05:00.771
and it's an average
velocity meters per 350,

05:01.634 --> 05:03.631
meters per minute.

05:03.631 --> 05:05.041
And we are done.
